.TH KBD_BACKLIGHT 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manuals"
.SH NAME
kbd_backlight \- get or set the keyboard backlight brightness level
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kbd_backlight
[\fIBRIGHTNESS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kbd_backlight
is a simple utility to control the intensity of the keyboard LEDs.
It writes a numerical value directly to the kernel's LED class interface.
.PP
If a numeric
.I BRIGHTNESS
argument is provided, the script sets the backlight to that level.
If no argument is provided, the script displays the current brightness level.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I BRIGHTNESS
An integer value representing the desired brightness level.
The range is hardware-dependent (commonly 0 to 3 or 0 to 255).
Providing a non-numeric value will result in an error
.SH SECURITY
This script uses
.MR sudo 1
in conjunction with
.MR tee 1
to gain the necessary write permissions for the
.I sysfs
directory. The user must have appropriate sudoers privileges to execute
this command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/leds/kbd_backlight/brightness
The kernel device interface used to control the keyboard LED hardware.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B kbd_backlight 3
Sets the keyboard backlight to level 3.
.TP
.B kbd_backlight
Turns the keyboard backlight off (defaults to 0).
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR sudo 8 ,
.MR tee 1 ,
.MR cat 1
